00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.269 align:start position:0%
 
good morning everyone  on behalf of the ukrainian community  here in victoria the ukrainian cultural  center  and the ukrainian canadian congress  victoria branch  i'd like to welcome you to the cultural  center and thank you all so much for  being here  we are truly truly humbled to be the  site of this visit and announcement  and i'd also like to recognize the  traditional territory before we begin  i'm going to acknowledge with respect  that we are on the traditional  territories of the luang and with  saanich first nations  and as a people who are  currently struggling for the territorial  integrity of our own homeland it is so  incredibly important to recognize the  territorial integrity of other  traditional homelands here that we have  the privilege to to live on  um  so i'd like to announce or sorry i'd  like to introduce the  minister  of national defense  to make an announcement  minister  [Applause]  good morning  i am honored to be here at the ukrainian  cultural center in victoria british  columbia  to meet and visit with the local  ukrainian canadian community and to  thank community organizers  who have been helping ukrainians fleeing  violence to resettle here in canada  over the past weeks  organizers right here in victoria have  raised approximately two hundred  thousand dollars to assist ukrainian  newcomers to canada they exemplify the  very best of canada and indeed canadians  when people need our help canadians pull  together  and stand with them  canada and ukraine are more than close  partners  we are family  completed  ukrainians  since the beginning of russia's illegal  invasion of ukraine in 2014  canada has been present to support our  ukrainian friends with comprehensive  military aid  in fact since 2015 the canadian armed  forces have trained over  33 000 members  of ukrainian troops  and it is heartening to see these troops  fighting today with such bravery and  dedication  last month my american counterpart  secretary of defense  austin convened over 40 of ukraine's  defense partners for a conference at  ramstein air base in germany to discuss  what more we could do collectively to  support ukraine's defense needs and  yesterday we met via video link for  another meeting of ukraine's defense  contact group  today i am here to announce the next  package of canadian military aid to  ukraine i can confirm that canada has  purchased over twenty thousand rounds of  one hundred and fifty five millimeter  artillery which is nato's standard  artillery caliber  this package will also include fuses and  charge bags at a cost of up to 98  million dollars  these rounds are compatible with  artillery guns provided by canada and  our allies including the m777 howitzers  that we have donated and which will be  crucial in ukraine's current fight to  defend its eastern territory work is  already underway to deliver this aid to  ukraine as quickly as possible  today's announcement builds on the  military aid that canada has dedicated  to ukraine since 2022 in february  canada's military aid to  ukraine has been comprehensive  we have supplied ukraine  with small arms  specialized equipment like cameras for  military drones  armored vehicles and the heavy artillery  guns i mentioned namely m triple seven  howitzers  and canada has trained ukrainian forces  in the use of these heavy artillery guns  building on the strong relationships our  forces developed with their ukrainian  counterparts through operation unifier  canadian aid continues to flow into  ukraine and we are working around the  clock to identify  and provide even more military aid to  ukraine  with the 500 million dollars that we  announced in budget 2022 for this  purpose  [Applause]  now when we last spoke  my ukrainian counterpart alexey reznikov  told me that canada has been very  helpful  in ukraine's fight against the russian  occupiers and that we are very grateful  that canada stands with us  and we will continue to do just that  conversations  putin's full-scale illegal and  unconscionable invasion of ukraine  cannot be allowed to succeed and it will  not  [Applause]  russian forces have been pushed back  keeve remains free and the maple leaf  flies over the streets of ukraine's  capital once again at our embassy  through military aid economic assistance  humanitarian aid and strong political  support at international forums canada  will continue to have ukraine's back  putin cannot  redraw maps to suit his own needs  sovereign nations cannot be erased from  the map  and the ukrainian people's basic right  to independence and self-determination  cannot be undermined without consequence  thank you merci  [Applause]  hello  um  i will say that canada and ukraine are  very close partners and allies and we  from the very beginning have been  responding to requests that ukraine has  consistently been in touch with us about  the prime minister  and president zielenski speak frequently  and i speak frequently with minister  aleksey reznikov about what continued  military aid we can provide  just a few weeks ago in kiev the prime  minister announced an additional 50  million dollars in military assistance  for ukraine including additional drone  cameras small arms satellite imagery and  m777 ammunition and this adds to the  over 130 million dollars in military aid  that we have already committed today's  announcement builds on those previous  announcements and in particular  canada's purchase of 20 000 rounds of  155 millimeter artillery which is nato's  standard artillery caliber is exactly  what ukraine has asked allies to provide  and is exactly what canada has sourced  and is contributing  that funding hasn't come fairly yet so  they're relying still on charity dollars  here raised as you mentioned in victoria  um  when will that um  yes so let me just take a step back and  speak about military housing as a  general matter  to be clear  across the country canadians are faced  with housing shortages and our  government has the national housing  strategy and committed additional funds  in budget 2022. in terms of military  members and their families  who make incredible sacrifices to serve  canada we will continue to take steps to  ensure that they are supported for  example in february 2021 we increased  military members rates of pay  to ensure alignment with increases  received by the federal public service  we also implemented an interim  relocation policy to enable remote work  options and we also ensure flexibility  for our members and their families when  they're being relocated and to ensure  the post living differential allowance  which is intended to help reduce  financial burdens  we have  the effective support for caf members  and their families and we are seeking to  address through that affordability  concerns we have more work to do in this  area we will continue to support  military members and their families  [Applause]  i would love to chat with families and  members here today if you have a moment  it would be my privilege to speak with  you individually thank you

